:: FathersBlessing
<h2 class="story-title">The Father's Blessing</h2>

When the sethani entered the Rang Mahal, a maidservant was massaging the thakur's feet. Thakur-sa had just drifted off to sleep.

When the maidservant saw a woman as beautiful as Gangaur standing in the doorway, she smiled, stopped rubbing his legs, and quietly took her leave.

The sethani sat at the foot of the bed and began rubbing her lover's legs.

All of a sudden, Thakur-sa woke up.

**Without opening his eyes, he said:**

"That's enough for now, **my daughter**. Time for you to sleep."

<div class="thought-box">
When she heard herself called *daughter*, the sethani's hands froze right where they were.
</div>

The thakur said again: "My daughter, aren't you listening? Have you fallen asleep while rubbing my legs?"

The thakur pulled his feet away. He heard the jingling of jewelry and sat up with a start. By the light of the hundred-wicked pilajota lamp, he saw this was the sethani!

But now that he had called her *daughter*, all the dirt and poison in his mind suddenly cleared.

"This must be what Bhagwan wishes," he said. "From today onwards, you will be my daughter in dharma."

He took a necklace from around his neck and presented it to her. "Accept this as you would in a farewell trousseau. Now don't wait any longer—the maidservants will get suspicious."

The daughter tried to stand but couldn't. All the stars had fallen from the sky in a single breath. She couldn't speak, as if a bitter tuharo fruit had caught in her throat.

